<messaging:emailTemplate subject=" {!relatedTo.NSP_AIMS_Client_Name__c} ({!relatedTo.NSP_AIMS_ClientNo__c}) - Critical Payroll Compliance Documentation  " recipientType="User" relatedToType="Implementation_Profile__c">
<messaging:HtmlEmailBody >
<html>
<body>
<c:InsperityEmailHeader ></c:InsperityEmailHeader>

<p style="color: #FF0000">INSTRUCTIONS: Please read through the email summary and edit as needed for this client. Create a new <br/>
email to the Payroll Contact. Copy and paste everything below the red line from this email into the new <br/>
email to the Payroll Contact.</p>
<p style="color: #FF0000">--------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>

<p> Dear {!relatedTo.NSP_PC_Client_Name__c},</p>

<p>I hope this message finds you well. To ensure we stay on track with your implementation timeline, maintain payroll compliance, and accurately process employee pay, please review the following items and provide the requested documentation at your earliest convenience. Your prompt attention to these matters is greatly appreciated, as I need these items before processing your first payroll.</p>


<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.NSP_Does_the_client_have_prior_wages__c,'Yes')}">
<p><strong>Prior Wage Data</strong><br/>
After processing your final payroll outside of Insperity, provide a year-to-date (YTD) report to prevent the restart of taxable wage bases, if appropriate under applicable law. This report must include:</p>
<p>
&nbsp;&nbsp;o <b>Federal Employer Identification Number (FEIN)</b> under which the wages were paid<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;o <b>Gross wages</b> for each employee<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;o <b>Itemized taxes</b> for each employee<br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;o <b>Itemized deductions</b> for each employee
</p>
</apex:outputPanel>

<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!AND(CONTAINS(relatedTo.Client_have_any_EEs_on_F1_or_J1_Visa_s__c,'Yes'),
     OR(IF(relatedTo.NSP_EE_Name__c!=Null,True,FALSE),
     IF(relatedTo.EE_Visa_Type__c!=Null,True,FALSE)))}">    
<p><strong>F1 or J1 Visa</strong><br/>
Provide a copy of the respective visa for:</p>
<c:NSP_EmployeeVisaCmp currentRecordId="{!relatedTo.Id}"/>
</apex:outputPanel>

<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Do_any_EEs_have_tax_levies__c, 'Yes')}">
<p><strong>Tax Levies</strong><br/>
1. Contact the levying agency for each employee with a levy.<br/>
2. Inform the levying agency that you are no longer paying wages to the employee.<br/>
3. Indicate that the tax levy must be transferred to Insperity.<br/>
4. Send the revised levy to <b>Insperity Attn: Garnishment Department, 19001 Crescent Springs Dr., Kingwood, TX 77339, Fax: 866-309-1267.</b></p>
<c:NSP_EmployeeLeviesCmp currentRecordId="{!relatedTo.Id}"/>
</apex:outputPanel> 

<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!AND(CONTAINS(relatedTo.Do_any_EEs_have_garnishments__c,'Yes'),
     IF(relatedTo.NSP_Employee_Names_List_garnishments__c!=Null,True,FALSE))}">
<p><strong>Garnishment Court Order</strong><br/>
Provide the most recent garnishment for:</p>
<c:NSP_EmployeeGarnishmentCmp currentRecordId="{!relatedTo.Id}"/>
</apex:outputPanel>

<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!OR(
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'AK'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'AR'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'CT'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'DE'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'IL'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'IA'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'KS'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'KY'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'ME'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MA'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MI'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MN'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MS'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'NE'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'NV'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'ND'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'OH'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'PA'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'RI'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'SC'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'SD'),
CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'TN'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'VT'),CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'WA'))}">
<p><strong>State Unemployment</strong><br/>
The below state(s) require unemployment wages and taxes to be reported under the client’s name. After wages are paid, a Payroll Tax Compliance Specialist will provide further instructions if needed. Please review <apex:outputLink value="https://portal.insperity.com/pcms/payroll_tax_guidelines" target="_parent"> Payroll Tax Guidelines page</apex:outputLink> for additional information on Insperity Premier. Please note: At your sole discretion, you may close an unemployment tax account, except for the below state(s). However, if you keep an unemployment tax account open, you must file all reports timely, even if they are zero reports.
</p>

<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'AK')}"><li>Alaska</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'AR')}"><li>Arkansas</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'CT')}"><li>Connecticut**</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'DE')}"><li>Delaware</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'IL')}"><li>Illinois</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'IA')}"><li>Iowa</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'KS')}"><li>Kansas</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'KY')}"><li>Kentucky</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'ME')}"><li>Maine</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MA')}"><li>Massachusetts**</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MI')}"><li>Michigan</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MN')}"><li>Minnesota</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'MS')}"><li>Mississippi</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'NE')}"><li>Nebraska</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'NV')}"><li>Nevada</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'ND')}"><li>North Dakota</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'OH')}"><li>Ohio</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'PA')}"><li>Pennsylvania</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'RI')}"><li>Rhode Island</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'SC')}"><li>South Carolina</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'SD')}"><li>South Dakota</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'TN')}"><li>Tennessee</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'VT')}"><li>Vermont</li></apex:outputPanel>
<apex:outputPanel rendered="{!CONTAINS(relatedTo.Employees_work_in_the_following_states__c ,'WA')}"><li>Washington**</li></apex:outputPanel>
<p><strong>**Paid Family Medical Leave (PFML)</strong> - These states also require Insperity to file our client’s name and EIN for PFML reporting.</p>  
</apex:outputPanel>


<p><strong>Regular Rate of Pay</strong></p>
<p>
Review the following resources to understand your responsibilities regarding Regular Rate of Pay (RRP) and the necessary calculations if a non-exempt hourly or salaried employee works overtime and receives additional compensation during the same pay period:
</p>
<p>
&nbsp;&nbsp;• <apex:outputLink value="https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/fact-sheets/23-flsa-overtime-pay" target="_parent"> Fact Sheet #23: Overtime Pay Requirements of the FLSA | U.S. Department of Labor</apex:outputLink> <br/>
&nbsp;&nbsp;• <apex:outputLink value="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-29/subtitle-B/chapter-V/subchapter-B/part-778#sg29.3.778_1106.sg1" target="_parent"> Code of Federal Regulations Part 778 -- Overtime Compensation</apex:outputLink>
</p>

<p>Insperity is here to help. Please let me know if I can provide further assistance.</p>



<p>Regards,<br/>
{!relatedTo.NSP_Payroll_Specialist__r.Name}<br/>
{!relatedTo.NSP_Payroll_Specialist__r.NSP_Job_Title__c}<br/>
{!relatedTo.NSP_Payroll_Specialist__r.NSP_Work_email__c}</p>
<c:InsperityEmailFooter ></c:InsperityEmailFooter> 
</body>
</html>
</messaging:HtmlEmailBody>
</messaging:emailTemplate>